<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Ms. Richards returns three months after her first zoledronic acid infusion. The evening after the infusion she had aching muscles and a temperature of 37.9 °C, which settled with acetaminophen and were gone on the third day; she has had no symptoms since. She has had no muscle cramps, tingling, jaw pain, or thigh or groin pain. She takes vitamin D3 1971 units a day and keeps her calcium at about 1200 mg a day from food. She does the home balance program three times a week, walks most days, and has had no falls. She came fasting this morning for her blood tests. She has had no alcohol. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Infusion reaction</td><td>Aches and 37.9 °C for two days after the dose, settled with acetaminophen</td></tr><tr><td>Drug safety</td><td>No cramps, tingling, jaw pain, or thigh or groin pain</td></tr><tr><td>Supplements and diet</td><td>D3 1971 units daily; calcium about 1200 mg a day from food</td></tr><tr><td>Falls</td><td>None; home balance program three times a week</td></tr><tr><td>Recovery</td><td>No alcohol; no cravings</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

<component>
  <section>
