    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.9" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Low bone mass with high fracture risk, on zoledronic acid (M85.89)</content>. Fasting CTX 190 pg/mL, 66 percent lower than the baseline of 560, showing the expected response. Calcium 9.3 mg/dL. The acute-phase reaction after the first dose was mild and brief and usually does not recur with later doses. No signs of osteonecrosis of the jaw or atypical femoral fracture. [S]<list><item>Continue vitamin D3 1971 units daily and calcium from food.</item><item>Second yearly dose in May after calcium, creatinine, and 25-hydroxyvitamin D.</item><item>DXA two years after starting; reassess for a drug holiday after the third yearly dose.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">History of falls (Z91.81)</content>. No falls in six months; balance gains kept up with the home program. [S]<list><item>Continue the home balance and strength program.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Alcohol use disorder in sustained remission (F10.21)</content>. No alcohol or cravings. Safety reviewed: no thoughts of suicide or self-harm; the 988 Suicide &amp; Crisis Lifeline is saved in her phone. [S]<list><item>Continue the recovery check at each visit.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Protocol monitoring: items the monitoring protocol calls for at this visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Measure</th><th>Interval</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Bone-turnover marker (fasting serum CTX)</td><td>Baseline, then 3 to 6 months after starting or changing therapy</td><td>Completed today</td><td>190 pg/mL, 66 percent below the baseline of 560; response and adherence confirmed</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Serum calcium</td><td>Before each zoledronic acid dose, and after the first dose if symptoms suggest hypocalcemia</td><td>Completed today</td><td>9.3 mg/dL, normal; checked with the CTX sample</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>25-hydroxyvitamin D</td><td>After repletion until 30 ng/mL or more; then yearly</td><td>Up to date</td><td>38 ng/mL in May; next with the pre-infusion tests in May</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Acute-phase reaction after zoledronic acid</td><td>After the first dose</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Aches and 37.9 °C for two days, settled with acetaminophen; acetaminophen offered again for the next dose</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Osteonecrosis of the jaw and atypical femoral fracture symptoms</td><td>At each visit on antiresorptive therapy</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No jaw pain or exposed bone; no thigh or groin pain; routine dental care twice a year</td></tr><tr><td>Imaging</td><td>Central DXA of the spine and hip</td><td>Every 1 to 2 years on therapy until stable, on the same scanner</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Due two years after starting therapy, on the same scanner</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Standing height by stadiometer</td><td>Yearly; vertebral imaging again if height falls 2 cm or more</td><td>Up to date</td><td>164.0 cm, unchanged</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Fall-risk screen</td><td>Yearly, and with any fall</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Timed Up and Go 9 seconds, tandem stance 20 seconds; no falls</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>FRAX 10-year fracture risk</td><td>At baseline, when risk factors change, and at the drug-holiday decision</td><td>Up to date</td><td>No change in risk factors; next at the drug-holiday decision</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Calcium intake assessment</td><td>At baseline and yearly</td><td>Up to date</td><td>About 1200 mg a day from food</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Drug-holiday eligibility</td><td>After 3 yearly zoledronic acid doses or 5 years of an oral bisphosphonate</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>One dose so far; reassess after the third yearly dose</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Balance and strength exercise program</td><td>With a history of falls or impaired balance</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Home program three times a week</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Recovery check (alcohol, cravings, stress)</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No alcohol; no cravings</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Suicide-risk review and safety plan, with the 988 Suicide &amp; Crisis Lifeline</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No thoughts of suicide or self-harm; the 988 Suicide &amp; Crisis Lifeline is saved in her phone</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Goal progress:</paragraph><list><item>Total calcium intake of about 1200 mg a day, mostly from food, by the four-week visit. Outcome by 1997-03-10: About 1200 mg a day from food by her own three-day food record [S]</item><item>25-hydroxyvitamin D of 30 ng/mL or more before the first infusion. Outcome by 1997-05-12: 24 ng/mL at intake and 38 ng/mL at three months [S]</item><item>First zoledronic acid dose by the three-month visit, with normal calcium and kidney function and a dental check done. Outcome by 1997-05-12: Given at three months after normal calcium (9.5 mg/dL) and eGFR (81) and a routine dental examination [S]</item><item>Complete the eight-week balance and strength program, with no falls through six months. Outcome by 1997-08-11: 16 of 16 sessions; Timed Up and Go 9 seconds and tandem stance 20 seconds at six months; no falls [S]</item><item>Serum CTX at least 30 percent lower three months after the first dose. Outcome by 1997-08-11: 560 pg/mL at baseline and 190 pg/mL at three months after the dose (66 percent lower) [S]</item><item>Sustained remission from alcohol use disorder throughout the episode. Outcome by 1997-08-11: No alcohol reported at any visit; AUDIT-C 0 at intake [S]</item></list><paragraph>Guideline basis: CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, osteoporosis monograph (2026); The clinician&apos;s guide to prevention and treatment of osteoporosis (2022); American Association of Clinical Endocrinologists/American College of Endocrinology Clinical Practice Guidelines for the Diagnosis and Treatment of Postmenopausal Osteoporosis, 2020 Update (2020); Pharmacological Management of Osteoporosis in Postmenopausal Women: An Endocrine Society Clinical Practice Guideline (2019); STEADI: Stopping Elderly Accidents, Deaths, and Injuries (2026); VA/DoD Clinical Practice Guideline for the Management of Substance Use Disorders (2021); VA/DoD Clinical Practice Guideline for Assessment and Management of Patients at Risk for Suicide (2024)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Adult preventive visit in October. Second zoledronic acid dose in May with pre-infusion tests. Call for jaw pain, thigh or groin pain, or any fall. Next scheduled visit 1997-10-06: adult preventive visit. [S]</paragraph></text>

